# A migration file is the thing that actually changes production, so a
# promotion PR (development -> main) that touches one should get a human read
# before merging -- see AGENTS.md "How production gets changed". This is
# documentation of that convention, not a GitHub-enforced gate: branch
# protection does not require Code Owner review, so it never blocks a merge.
#
# It also won't notify the reviewer named below if they're the PR's author --
# GitHub never auto-requests a review from someone on their own PR. On a
# single-maintainer repo where every promotion PR is opened by that person,
# this shows up as an informational "Code owners" note on the PR, not an
# actual review request. Reading the migration diff before merging is still
# on the merging human; nothing here enforces it.
